[h1]Updates in this patch:[/h1]
[list]
[*] The target score in Domination mode has been increased from 250 to 500 points. This change should balance gameplay and give both teams a better shot at turning the match in their favour.
[*] The custom graffiti of the winner of our Launch Giveaway – Xjac0bmichaelX – has popped up on the Polis arena. 
[*] The size of the Genesis arena has been reduced by 25%. 
[/list]

[img]https://steamcdn-a.akamaihd.net/steamcommunity/public/images/clans/30211483/0fd1b1d6f4bb8b1d79f071bbc873e7f6803d3404.png[/img]

[h1]We fixed these bugs:[/h1] 
[list]
[*] Missing colliders have been added to Genesis; 
[*] The Pineapple is now actually nerfed – pellet damage has been reduced from 40 to 20;
[*] The controller shader and button layout bugs in the tutorial;
[*] All logic errors in the customisation menu, incl. numbering and tab sequences;
[*] Several bugs affecting communication between the game and server;
[*] The bug that disabled the microphones of all of the players in the match after a map vote;
[*] The bug that would display the same amount of gained XP for several matches regardless of how much the player actually gained XP in each individual match; 
[*] The bug that caused the game to display incorrect scores in Team Deathmatch. 
[*] The faulty control points in Domination Mode on the Genesis arena. 
[/list]

[h1]General Note from the Devs![/h1] 
We are aware that in certain cases when a player joins a match, the audio from other players will be muted even though the mic symbol shows them talking. The player's own audio is still heard by the other players. 
Fixing this bug will take a bit more time and we didn't want to delay the patch any further. A quick fix for the bug is closing the app (only leaving the match will not do the trick) and reopening it. 
We will have this bug fixed in the next patch.

[h1]Patch 15 is all cute and tiny, so let's get into it![/h1]

Frist off, we realized a couple patches back that the two-handed mode for our Sniper Rifle and Locust minigun has remained a mystery to a lot of players. As such, we added a visual prompt for two-hand use when the Sniper Rifle and Locust are equipped for the first time. The prompt appears only once per session and can be disabled in the Options menu.

Secondly, let's be honest, our characters flight looked a bit stiff. This patch brings character movement animations, which should result in more realistic looking flying.

Lastly, bot mode has been the bane of many of our players. To make the bots less deadly, we decreased the bots' fire rate by 50% and increased their fire spread by 100%.

[h1]Patch 15 includes the following bug fixes:[/h1] 
[list]
[*]Eliminated a bug that allowed for only 9 players in a 10-player match;
[*]Fixed some collision meshes that caused weird bounce angles for grenades on the Egypt map;
[*]Got rid of a tutorial bug that caused button layout errors on Oculus controllers;
[*]And another bug that caused the tutorial menu to move after using the rotate buttons on Oculus;
[*]The shockwave ability now does damage to bots in the tutorial; 
[*]Fixed the problem with the incorrect password popup window, which caused it to appear behind the main menu when you entered the wrong password for a private match;
[*]And got rid of a bug that caused the player's arms to freeze in a fixed position after being killed while holding a weapon with two hands.
[/list]

And there you have it, patch 15. ːsteamhappyː

Everybody makes the occasional blunder, and it seems we may have made some in yesterday's patch. 

We're super grateful that you guys are so vocal and honest with us. We couldn't do this without your feedback!  

So here we go:
[list]
[*]The reload time of the shotgun has been nerfed back to 2 secs from 1.5 secs;
[*]The distance of the grappling hook has been buffed up to 70 metres. However, we did nerf the grapple pull acceleration by a factor of 0.3 to limit the maximum speed that can be achieved;
[*]We fixed a bug that calculated incorrect headshot values for all raycast weapons;
[*]And the Game End Menu animations have currently been disabled due to several bugs. 
[/list]

Be sure to holler at us if you notice some other bugs! Thanks for being awesome! :)

